From 3c697ce21088c680a64151f34d1189345d2985e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NEMO Phase II executor <executor@nemo.local>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 12:49:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Phase II: coagulation-ON init+integration works on a
 dust-only fixture

Brings the coagulation path (default-off infrastructure from 1fe51f1) to a
running, validated state on a small ice-free, chemistry-free fixture -- the
fast vehicle the full 1414-species network cannot provide (it is too slow to
integrate here). Coagulation-OFF remains byte-identical: jac_weight_check is
unchanged (13450 entries, worst reldiff 1.8006e-3, 0 weight bugs).

New fixture tests/fixture_dust_coag/ (generator: scripts-free, see commit body):
  16-bin derived mass-doubling grid (a_min 1e-6, a_max 3.2e-5, rho 3), MRN IC,
  coagulation=1 constant kernel K0=1e-9, is_grain_reactions=0, ice-free 2-element
  (H,He) network, empty reaction/surface files. Coag count fires correctly:
  120 pair reactions, 16 top-bin overflow pairs skipped (136 = 16*17/2).

Result on the fixture (both -O0/bounds and -O2):
  * mass Sum m_k n_k conserved to ~5e-16 (machine precision) -- GATE (a) passes;
  * total grain number decreases (N/N0=0.977 at 100 yr), the two smallest bins
    deplete and every larger bin grows -- correct coagulation + Podolak/Brauer
    mass redistribution.

Code changes, each guarded so the stock/default build is byte-identical
(coagulation flag off, or nb_chemistry_reactions==nb_reactions, or a resolved
index that is always positive in a full network):
  * input_output: read `coagulation` as a 0/1 switch (matches is_* convention);
    accept an empty grain_species.in (ice-free networks have no surface species);
    bound the reaction reorder + its completeness check to nb_chemistry_reactions
    (coag block is appended pre-sorted after read_reactions).
  * gasgrain: bound the four init_reaction_rates chemistry sweeps to
    nb_chemistry_reactions (coag rates come from dust_coagulation_set_rates);
    when coagulation is on, turn absent reaction-type ranges into the empty
    do-loop range [1,0] so the many `do J=type_id_start(T),type_id_stop(T)` rate
    loops don't run at J=0 on a chemistry-free network; tiling validator now keys
    on stop==0 (treats [0,0] and [1,0] identically as "type absent").
  * ode_solver: bound the accretion-prefactor sweep to nb_chemistry_reactions
    (coag reactions have no reactant_1_idx and don't accrete).
  * main: guard the self-shielding column densities on a resolved species index
    so a reduced network doesn't index abundances(0); values are only consumed by
    H2/CO/N2 self-shielding, which is absent here.
  * dustevolution: assign each coag reaction a unique high-based REACTION_ID so
    the duplicate-ID preliminary test doesn't see them as clashing entries.

preliminary_test is left off in the fixture: the remaining preliminary checks
(adsorption/grain-equivalent/production-destruction) validate gas-grain chemistry
that a dust-only network intentionally lacks; the coag-relevant tiling validator
passes with it on. Next: monodisperse IC + K0 tuned to the knee for the analytic
M0-decay gate (b1), and wiring the dropped-flux diagnostic into output.
